147: ## 4. What Was Enhanced
148: 
149: ### 4.1 CalendarStrip — Multi-Dot Calendar
150: 
151: **Current:** Shows a single green dot if `goalDates.has(dateStr)`.
152: 
153: **Enhanced:** Shows up to 3 colored dots per date:
154: - **Goal dots:** Colored by category (work=pink, personal=violet, health=emerald, learning=cyan, finance=amber, relationships=rose)
155: - **Deadline dot:** Rose `#f43f5e` (diamond shape, not circle)
156: - **Reminder dot:** Amber `#fbbf24` (smaller circle)
157: 
158: **Implementation:**
159: ```tsx
160: // In CalendarStrip, replace the single dot with:
161: <span className="flex gap-0.5 mt-0.5">
162:   {getDotsForDate(dateStr).slice(0, 3).map((dot, i) => (
163:     <span
164:       key={i}
165:       className={dot.shape === 'diamond' ? 'w-1 h-1 rotate-45' : 'w-1 h-1 rounded-full'}
166:       style={{ background: dot.color }}
167:     />
168:   ))}
169: </span>
170: ```
171: 
172: **Data flow:** GoldPage passes `radarMarks` (already computed) down to `CalendarStrip` as a new prop `marks: Map<string, RadarMark[]>`. The strip also uses `weekGoals` to derive category-colored goal dots.
173: 
174: **Today indicator:** Keep the existing violet dot in the corner, but change to amber to match the page accent.
175: 
176: ### 4.2 WeekBoard — Enhanced Habit Grid
177: 
178: **Current:** Shows habit dot-chips and daily goal count.
179: 
180: **Enhanced:**
181: - **Deadline indicators:** Small rose diamond in the top-right of a day cell if that day has a deadline
182: - **Reminder indicators:** Small amber dot above the day number if reminders exist
183: - **Goal count:** Shows not just "3 daily" but a mini breakdown: "2 work · 1 health" using category dots
184: - **Click behavior:** Clicking a day navigates to it (existing). Clicking a habit dot toggles it (existing). **New:** Clicking a deadline indicator opens the deadline in `DeadlineRadar`.
185: 
186: ### 4.3 Goal-Schedule Linking
187: 
188: **New field usage:** `ScheduleEntry.goal_id` already exists in the types. Now it's surfaced in the UI.
189: 
190: **In ScheduleCard:**
191: - When rendering a block, if `entry.goal_id` exists, look up the goal in `linkedGoals`
192: - Show: `Serves: [category dot] Goal Title` beneath the time/location row
193: - The left rail color of the block defaults to the linked goal's category color (if no explicit `color` is set)
194: - Clicking the goal name sets `selectedDate` to the goal's date and scrolls to the goal list
195: 
196: **In GoalCard:**
197: - If the goal has `linkedScheduleId`, show a small calendar icon with "Scheduled" badge
198: - Clicking it highlights the schedule block
199: 
200: **In CriteriaBuilder:**
201: - New optional field: "Link to schedule block" — a dropdown of existing schedule entries for the selected day
202: - When a goal is linked to a schedule block, the block's `goal_id` is updated via `onUpdateSchedule`
203: 
204: ### 4.4 DeadlineRadar — Goal-Aware
205: 
206: **Enhanced:**
207: - Clicking a deadline date in the month grid not only navigates to that date but also **filters the goal list** to show goals due on that date
208: - Deadlines that are linked to goals (via `goal_id` in the deadline type, or matching title) show the goal's category color instead of generic rose
209: - Countdown list items show a "related goals" count if any goals share that date
210: 
211: ### 4.5 BellBoard — Goal-Aware Reminders
212: 
213: **Enhanced:**
214: - Reminders can be created from a goal card via a new "Remind me" action
215: - Reminders with `goal_id` show the goal title and category dot
216: - Quick-add chips include "Tomorrow" and "Next week" (existing) plus **"Goal deadline"** (sets due date to the selected goal's deadline)
